<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pemex</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Petróleos Mexicanos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pemex (Petróleos Mexicanos) is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>'s state oil company, created in 1938 after President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lazaro-cardenas">Lázaro Cárdenas</a> expropriated the foreign oil companies. It held a monopoly over oil production for most of its history, and its revenues long financed a large share of the federal budget. Discoveries such as the Cantarell field made it one of the world's largest oil producers.</p></div>
